It is a modified copy of the `runtime_image` component from ESPHome 2026.9.0
(https://github.com/esphome/esphome), Copyright (c) 2019 ESPHome, and it keeps
ESPHome's split licensing:

  *.cpp, *.h                       GPL-3.0-or-later
  *.py                             MIT

The full upstream license text is in ../../LICENSES/ESPHome-LICENSE.txt.

Modification vs upstream:

  `RuntimeImage::end_decode()` and `RuntimeImage::release()` destroy the decoder
  object instead of retaining it for reuse. This restores ESPHome 2026.7.4's
  decoder lifetime while preserving the completed image buffer. It prevents a
  pool of distinct RuntimeImage instances from retaining one decoder per cached
  image.

Everything else is unchanged.